ESLint: 9.39.4

A configuration object specifies rule "react-hooks/set-state-in-effect", but could not find plugin "react-hooks".

Common causes of this problem include:

1. The "react-hooks" plugin is not defined in your configuration file.
2. The "react-hooks" plugin is not defined within the same configuration object in which the "react-hooks/set-state-in-effect" rule is applied.

